  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_acdrop",
      "name": {
        "en": "Aciddrop's Badge",
        "zh": "酸糖证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "original",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Aciddrop has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for inflicting physical casualties with precision on enemies at close range.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Heavyshooter responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员酸糖擅长射击近距离敌人造成精准物理杀伤\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使重射手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_acdrop",
      "name": {
        "en": "'Freedom, Onion Rings, and Me'",
        "zh": "“自由、洋葱圈和我”",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_acdrop",
      "description": {
        "en": "They crossed the line.\nThe Siracusans... and Victorians... and Bolívarians. They injured an innocent child. And they stopped up the station door with bills... Should've known Columbia was like this. Always has been.\nNo one who could've helped that kid. Went by the nickname 'Aciddrop.' Got into competitions. Glowed like the sun on the outer dunes back then. Now she caught Oripathy. Whereabouts... unknown. I wind this tape up, that marks one month she's been missing.\nStill remember how I taught her to use a crossbow. Spark in her eyes, same as my wife and kids. Touched your heart some more than a breeze in the woods, and my girl—girls—[CHUCKLE]—I thought to myself back then how I pretty much had two goddamn daughters. 'Aciddrop.' She was like part of our family. Like candy. Sometimes her father came, checked in on her. Gaulish man, built strong. Nothing but guilt and love in his eyes whenever he looked at his daughter. He and I drank. He said he didn't know how to be a good father. Could've said the same myself.\nUsed to figure with how our families knew each other, be one of the few fancy things in my old age, but that all changed. Overnight. Kid, uh... left two skateboards here with me. The ones I 'confiscated.' Dumped them in the junk room too. Rolled right under that army sword from Bolívar.\nI'm just an old guy. Saw these things happen before—never concerned me then. Wanted to do something... only today decided what. I know, look at me, death of a salesman. Best decision maker zero years running. Heh.\n[SILENCE]\nTaping two copies of this. Remember to send one to the kid if anyone finds her. I'll teach you how to fry onion rings for it. Secret's in the cheese.\n[SILENCE]\nThey've got the smarts to stick with their own. Not much chance I come out on top. Feel sorry for my girl. Her dad shouldn't be taking a risk like this. Makes me glad, though... I fessed up about all this and she was in tears. Gave me the go-ahead.\n[SILENCE]\nHey, kid. My daughter's all grown up now. How about you? Where you at?\nNo matter where you are, I bet you'll get along just fine.\nGangs. Hah. They gonna be scarier than the Steam Knights? Fire raining from the Witch King's spire?\n[SILENCE, POURING LIQUOR]\nRemember this, kid.\n'Cheers to freedom, cheers to onion rings, and cheers to me.'\n—Video cassette, previously held under strict safekeeping at a police station, sent to Rhodes Island after a case of station theft. Sender marked 'Onion Ring Alliance.'",
        "zh": "他们越界了。\n那些叙拉古人，还有维多利亚人、玻利瓦尔人，他们伤害了无辜的孩子，还用钞票堵死了警察局的大门……我早该知道，哥伦比亚就是这样，一直都是。\n谁都没能帮到那个女孩。在用“酸糖”这个绰号参加比赛的时候，她就像是沙丘那头的太阳那么闪耀。现在，她感染了矿石病，下落不明。到录下这盘录像带为止，她已经失踪一个月了。\n我还记得我怎么教她用弩，她的眼睛里有像我妻子那样的活力，那是比林地的清风还要动人的活力，而我的女儿——女儿，呵呵，我那时还在想，我竟然有了两个女儿。“酸糖”，她就像是我们家庭的一员，像颗糖。她的父亲偶尔来看她，那是个健硕的高卢男人，他看着女儿时，眼里只有愧疚和爱。他和我喝酒，他说他不知道怎么做一个好父亲。我又何尝不是呢？\n我曾以为我们两家的关系会是我后半生为数不多的点缀，但这一切都变了。一夜之间。那个孩子，她在我这里留下了两块滑板。是我“没收”来的。还放在杂物间里，那把玻利瓦尔军刀的下面。\n我只是个老家伙，我曾经眼睁睁看着那些事发生——无动于衷。我想做点什么……而我今天才决定做点什么。碌碌无为，优柔寡断，呵。\n……（沉默）\n录像带有两盘，如果谁找到了那个孩子，记得给她寄一份。回头教你怎么炸洋葱圈，秘诀是乳酪。\n……（沉默）\n他们懂得如何党同伐异，我的胜算不大。我对不起我的女儿，她的父亲不该冒这个险，但我也很高兴……因为在我坦白了这一切后，她哭着赞同了我。\n……（沉默）\n嘿，孩子。我的女儿已经长大了，那你呢？你在哪？\n无论你在哪里，你都会好好活着吧。\n黑帮，哈，他们有蒸汽骑士那么可怕吗？和巫王高塔倾泻而下的火焰比呢？\n……（倒酒声）\n孩子，记住。\n“一杯敬自由，一杯敬洋葱圈，一杯敬我。”\n——一盘录像带，此物曾被严格保管在某地警局，在某次警局遭窃后，寄到了罗德岛。寄信人是“洋葱圈同盟”。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
